[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139271,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Leiomyoma is a benign tumour of smooth muscle.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139272,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8890/0 Leiomyoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139273,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F36.Y &amp; XH4CY6 Other specified benign neoplasm of eye or ocular adnexa &amp; Leiomyoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139274,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139275,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139276,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Leiomyomas have been reported in the orbit, eyelid {8963938;20966798;23929515}, conjunctiva {27994813;27993264;30454719;14516824}, and caruncle {9881563}, and intraocularly in the iris, ciliary body, and choroid (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/65/255\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Mesectodermal leiomyoma</em>). Orbital leiomyomas may be located in any area of the orbit, including the orbital apex with intracranial extension, or inferior orbit with extension into the paranasal sinuses {14189707;15677948;16033356;1894345;4361898;14998695;11136988;10202288}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139277,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital leiomyomas may cause proptosis, diplopia, deviation of the globe, and pain {15677948;14189707;11136988;28151824}. There may be swelling of the eyelids, conjunctiva {27994813}, and caruncle {9881563} with limited ocular motility.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139278,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are &lt;&nbsp;25&nbsp;cases of documented orbital leiomyoma {15677948;15921744;16033356;16286632;19273932;22384155;28151824;29276593}. The mean age is 38&nbsp;years (range: 3&ndash;74&nbsp;years) and there is a slight male predominance. There are 4&nbsp;cases of conjunctival leiomyomas {27994813;27993264;30454719;14516824}, 1&nbsp;of caruncular leiomyoma {9881563}, and 3&nbsp;of eyelid leiomyomas {8963938;20966798;23929515}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139279,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not known</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139280,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital leiomyoma is thought to arise from the smooth muscle cells of orbital vessels or from M&uuml;ller muscle cells {1200096}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139281,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital leiomyomas are usually firm, well circumscribed but unencapsulated, and lobulated; cut sections typically show a firm, whorled, white surface with solid areas, sometimes with calcification {15677948;14998695}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139282,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ocular leiomyomas are composed of intersecting fascicles of spindled cells with blunt-ended cigar-shaped nuclei and eosinophilic cytoplasm. There is no atypia or necrosis.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>Spindle cells are positive for SMA, desmin, and h-caldesmon, and negative for S100 {15677948;14998695;19273932}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>Other benign spindle cell tumours that occur in the orbit should be considered, such as neurofibroma, schwannoma, and solitary fibrous tumour {14998695}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139283,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No information has been reported on orbital leiomyoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139284,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139285,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> morphology of intersecting fascicles of spindled cells with blunt-ended cigar-shaped nuclei and eosinophilic cytoplasm; no atypia or necrosis.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> expression of SMA, h-caldesmon, and desmin; no staining for HMB45, cytokeratin, or S100.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139286,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139287,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 254,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital leiomyomas are benign, but there can be destruction of the orbital bone {22384155} and local recurrence due to incomplete removal {434098;15677948;1200096;11136988}. Two reported cases developed intracranial extension {11136988;1200096}, and one&nbsp;case transformed to a malignant sarcoma possibly due to radiotherapy {1200096}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]